## Grow it

A new feature is a new file under `src/` (its steps) and one under `app/` (its
routes and jobs); `operonx add` writes both, and past ~300 lines a file splits
into a folder (see `AGENTS.md`). Its tests go in `tests/<feature>/`, and
`app/main.py` gets one more import.
`operonx init . --http` (or `--web`, `--deploy`) adds a part later. Read
`AGENTS.md` and `.operonx/guide/README.md` first.
